From 6a2402e012d1e44c905afca1793d506a695ac64d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:53:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 62/64] CPU monitor: note that it reads a little low (a
 comment)

The calls of the audio routine that render nothing aren't counted as busy (fac1dfe7), but they take time: those that
find too little due and those that only write out samples rendered ahead before. In the emulator (tests/sdload S2
idle) about 2,200 such calls a second of a few hundred instructions each, ~0.3 % of the CPU the monitor doesn't show.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
---
 src/deluge/processing/engines/cpu_stats_core.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/deluge/processing/engines/cpu_stats_core.cpp b/src/deluge/processing/engines/cpu_stats_core.cpp
index e761f6cc..4977fa4d 100644
--- a/src/deluge/processing/engines/cpu_stats_core.cpp
+++ b/src/deluge/processing/engines/cpu_stats_core.cpp
@@ -134,7 +134,10 @@ void Collector::routineDone(uint32_t now, uint32_t sampleCounter, uint32_t voice
 	uint32_t samples = sampleCounter - routineSamplesStart_;
 	busyTotal_ += ticks; // Wraps, which is fine for differences
 	// mastertune-v17: a call that rendered nothing (nothing due yet, or less than the minimum window at light load, see
-	// AudioEngine's kMinSamplesDue) isn't rendering: it doesn't count towards the load shown
+	// AudioEngine's kMinSamplesDue) isn't rendering: it doesn't count towards the load shown. Its time is still spent,
+	// though, and so are the calls that only write out samples rendered ahead before: the load shown reads a little low
+	// by those (a few hundred instructions each; in the emulator, tests/sdload S2 idle, ~2,200 such calls a second,
+	// ~0.3 % of the CPU)
 	if (samples != 0) {
 		acc_.busyTicks += ticks;
 	}
